WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:09.384
We all understand that
she sat down on the bus.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.391
The narrow narrative of her

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:18.393
just on one day did something,

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:19.352
couldn't be further 
from the truth.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.440
Often, the man is out front,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.983
and you never 
hear about the wife.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.568
Here, the reverse is true.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.612
She was considered a threat,

00:00:29.612 --> 00:00:31.906
espousing radical views.

00:00:31.906 --> 00:00:33.491
If they could see her

00:00:33.491 --> 00:00:35.285
talking about the 
Republic of New Africa,

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.162
her out there with the Panthers.

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:38.204
 Then they would understand

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.956
the real Rosa Parks.

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:40.915
But they might have been

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:42.000
just a little frightened.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.003
She has been an activist

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:46.212
for over three decades.

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:48.256
For Ms. Parks,
 it was especially dangerous.

00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.300
Fighting on issues that are

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.385
still very much 
at the forefront.

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:55.096
She never gave up.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:56.765
She lit the torch

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.683
to the next generation.

